"Fix finding B2 (U2 review R-12): a completed password reset must clear the failed-sign-in lockout even when ending the other sessions fails. In src/identity/reset.ts, completePasswordReset updates the password, then removes the other sessions (up to 3 attempts of sessions_remove), and when that fails it signs the new session out, emits follow_up_failed and returns terminalFailure(RESET_SESSIONS_NOT_ENDED) BEFORE calling sign_in_attempt_clear. A person who was locked out is told to sign in with the new password but may still be refused for up to 15 minutes. Change: call sign_in_attempt_clear (same arguments as today: keyed email hash of normalizeEmail(session.email), p_user_id) right after the password update succeeded and before the session removal, so the lockout is cleared in both outcomes; keep the rest of the behaviour (retries, follow_up_failed event, sign-out, RESET_SESSIONS_NOT_ENDED result, reset_used event only on full success) unchanged. A failure of the clear call itself must not change the result (same best-effort behaviour as today). Tests: colocated unit test in src/identity (look for the existing reset test file) proving that a reset whose session removal fails still calls sign_in_attempt_clear and still returns the same terminal failure, that the clear happens before the session removal, and that the success path is unchanged. Record the accepted limit in aidlc/spaces/default/intents/261012-real-backend-local/follow-ups/minor-findings-plan.md under B2: other sessions of the account can stay open up to 30 days when their removal fails; owner: the repository owner (Botond). Mark B2 done there. Source: plan group B2 of that file. Skip Reverse Engineering (the person already decided that for these fixes)."
